189	/**
190	 * Whether the at-most-one-turn-per-node guard should be released.
191	 *
192	 * One ending holds it: work is still actively going, possibly on a different node
193	 * entirely, under this one. Every other ending has handed back — to a person, or to
194	 * nobody — and a node nothing is working on must not stay locked.
195	 *
196	 * The mechanism that enacts this is the `atomaton/in-progress` label, in
197	 * `entrypoints/machinery/manage_in_progress_label.ts`. It is deliberately not named
198	 * here: the rule is about turns and the label is one way to persist it.
